AAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d558d357db0715915bc4046d4960e35ef175380ad131532a1f8609e03f3d9163","event_uuid":"4c2b4444-d593-45d9-abff-74a9962b0c34","position":{"commit_sha":"280ec6d582f705ef9ecaf2521724a7641a0fb821","position":"1786825119221632001-4c2b4444-d593-45d9-abff-74a9962b0c34"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation landed for review as Gerrit change 1818 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1818), commit 8b05e976fa, worktree locust-autoresume.\n\nWhat was built (exactly the v6 design):\n- NEW src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py: verify_with_auto_resume — the bounded resumption loop, extracted as a helper along the existing call seam so _completion_precheck stays at its frozen complexity ceiling and close_precheck.py under the 800-LOC cap. close_precheck._completion_precheck's llm.verify_completion call site now calls the helper (the ONE seam shared by CLI/MCP/library via transition_close.close_ticket); gate_dispatch/CompletionAgentStep untouched.\n- Qualification REUSES completion_reconcile._insufficiency_only unchanged (asserted by a counting-wrapper test); no schema/prompt/model-facing changes.\n- Bounds: new verify.auto_resume_max config key (default 2; 0 disables; _as_int minimum=0; documented in docs/config.md) AND strict progress — a resumption dispatches only while the prior attempt strictly increased the cache-credited PASS count (seeded:true + met:true criteria records); zero progress stops early.\n- Trail: per attempt {attempt, cache_credited, remaining_unmet} attached to the verdict when a resumption ran (single-attempt verdicts keep their exact prior shape), carried onto the durable COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar (both PASS and FAIL branches of build_payload), and the refusal message states the resumption count + per-attempt counts.\n- Tests: tests/unit/test_close_autoresume_b5f8.py (17) — insufficiency-only resumes / refutation fails fast / plain PASS / zero-unmet FAIL, predicate reuse, max bound + attempts-count message, 0 disables, unchanged-count early stop, progress-then-stall = exactly one extra attempt, same pinned --ref on every attempt, trail on emitted FAIL sidecar + resumed PASS, config default/coercion, and a library-path close (rebar.transition -> close_ticket) exercising the shared seam.\n\nGates: make lint clean (complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0), make typecheck clean, full tests/unit green (10650 passed; pre-existing failures on this host were traced to harness-injected GIT_CONFIG safe.bareRepository=explicit, not the change — they pass with that env removed, on main too).\n\nAlso: file_impact refreshed to the actually-touched paths (the previously recorded workflow/completion_* paths were from a superseded plan revision; the v6 description's close_precheck seam is what landed). Frontier-handoff out-of-scope work parked as idea ticket daemonic-rounded-gnu (e82c-dd27-e3e8-4bb5), linked discovered_from this ticket.\n\nNext: await LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on change 1818, Submit, then close this ticket.","timestamp":1786822069750301001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close-out verification against MERGED main (Gerrit 1818 merged as 155a8001bb; worktree reset to origin/main = 80a69b0967). All 9 AC boxes verified and ticked:\n- Merged commit touches exactly the 7 recorded file_impact paths (git show --name-only 155a8001bb) — no expansion needed; no changes under llm/schemas or llm/reviewers (no schema/prompt change).\n- tests/unit/test_close_autoresume_b5f8.py: 16/16 pass at merged HEAD — covers predicate reuse (counting wrapper on completion_reconcile._insufficiency_only), the four qualification cases, real-seam call-count + same-ref binding, auto_resume_max bound (default 2, 0 disables) + attempts-count message, the three progress cases, per-attempt trail on sidecar verdict + close output, and the library-path close through transition_close.close_ticket.\n- verify.auto_resume_max wired: _config_schema.py:266 (default 2), _config_sections.py coercer (min 0), docs/config.md:107.\n- Frontier-handoff idea ticket daemonic-rounded-gnu (e82c-dd27-e3e8-4bb5) in idea status, linked discovered_from.\n- Merged via Gerrit = LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 (lint/typecheck green in CI).\nDescription edit staled the plan attestation; re-ran review-plan: PASS, 0 blocking (3 deferred advisory triage entries), signed at verified-at-sha 80a69b0967; --status now reports certified. Ticket left in_progress for the operator's close.","timestamp":1786824475936137001}],"created_at":1786759964065889001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"56df6082-090e-4b85-abbb-e74b27fc9fa2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8d74-2c9f-c98f-4f0b"},{"link_uuid":"456d9160-944d-42a0-bf4c-209b9f41c536","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b4be-0ed8-22cb-4b01"},{"link_uuid":"161ce5b0-f924-45cd-baab-7326d5486e3e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"66ac-42d2-c56f-4b1d"}],"description":"## Why\nWhen the completion verifier fails a close with \"insufficient evidence\" because the evidence search EXHAUSTED its step budget without refuting any criterion, the correct next action is mechanical: run it again. The verdict cache (Gerrit 1796) banks per-criterion PASSes at finalize even on overall FAIL, so a re-run seeds the credited criteria and spends its whole budget on the formerly-insufficient ones. This was demonstrated live (2026-08-14, ticket deadbeat-warlike-ostrich / 8d74): first close FAILed on exhaustion; an identical re-run closed clean with zero operator-added evidence. Operator ruling: bounded-search exhaustion is the gate's problem to resolve, not the operator's — the gate should auto-resume instead of demanding a human retype the same command.\n\n## Mechanism (maps to existing callables only)\nA resumption is a WHOLE-VERIFIER RE-RUN — exactly what the manual 8d74 re-close did — not a partial continuation. No new verification entry point:\n1. The resumption loop lives at the shared close-gate verification seam: `close_precheck._completion_precheck` (src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:497), specifically wrapping its `llm.verify_completion(...)` invocation (:638) and the verdict inspection that follows. This IS the shared seam — CLI, MCP, and library closes all flow through `rebar.transition` -> transition.py:23 -> `transition_close.close_ticket` (:454 calls `_completion_precheck`) -> that one call site. `gate_dispatch.produce_completion_verdict` / `CompletionAgentStep` are verdict PRODUCERS inside `verify_completion` and are NOT touched.\n2. Classification: a FAIL qualifies for auto-resume ONLY when it is insufficiency-only. The framework ALREADY computes exactly this: `_insufficiency_only(result)` (src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py:115) is True when every unmet criterion carries the framework-derived `evidence_sufficient: false` marker (set by the banking/assembly seams; reconcile derives and strips model-minted markers at :198-210, so a model cannot mint it) and at least one unmet record exists; an unmet record WITHOUT the marker is a genuine refutation → no resume. This ticket REUSES that predicate unchanged — no new schema field, no model-facing vocabulary, no prompt change. Existing consumers of the signal (completion_reconcile derivation :198, `_insufficiency_only` :115, completion_sidecar payload passthrough :382, completion_tool_policy, the finalizer prompt's banked-evidence rule) are enumerated in the change and stay untouched; the resumption loop is a NEW caller of the existing predicate.\n3. On qualification: re-invoke `verify_completion` with the same args/ref. The verdict cache seeds credited PASSes (existing behavior, no change needed); the fresh budget concentrates on remaining criteria (budget derivation unchanged — `verify_step_floor` stays parameterized on the total criteria count; concentration is emergent from cache hits consuming ~0 steps, as observed in the 8d74 live run).\n4. Bounded by count AND by progress. Count: `verify.auto_resume_max` resumptions per close invocation, default 2, 0 disables. Progress: a resumption is only dispatched when the just-finished attempt made progress — its cache-credited PASS count strictly exceeds the attempt before it (the first FAIL's credited count is the baseline). A zero-progress attempt means the next re-run would be an identical spin (same seeded cache, same budget, same remainder), so the loop stops early and surfaces the failure even with resumptions remaining. Each attempt logged to the ticket trail (comment or verdict metadata): attempt number, criteria credited-from-cache count, criteria remaining.\n5. Overall outcome: PASS on any attempt → close proceeds. Still exhausted after the bounded resumptions → the existing failure surface, with the message stating auto-resume was attempted N times (operator sees honest state).\n\n## Out of scope (split to child idea ticket)\nSearch-frontier handoff (steering a resumption away from already-searched places / toward where credited evidence was found) requires an argument-level tool-call transcript the verifier telemetry does not currently carry. That capability question — and the extractor design on top of it — is a separate idea ticket linked discovered_from this one; THIS ticket's resumption passes no frontier and needs no fallback (cache seeding alone proved sufficient live).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Qualification is `_insufficiency_only` (completion_reconcile.py:115) REUSED — asserted by test that the resumption loop calls it (no parallel reimplementation); no schema/prompt changes (diff-scope test or review assertion).\n- [x] Auto-resume triggers only on insufficiency-only FAILs: unit tests cover (a) all-unmet carry evidence_sufficient:false → resumes; (b) any unmet without the marker (refutation) → fails fast, no resume; (c) plain PASS → no resume; (d) FAIL with zero unmet records → no resume.\n- [x] Resumption re-invokes the existing `verify_completion` entry (asserted via call-count on the real seam), with the same ref binding (`--ref` closes resume against the same pinned ref).\n- [x] Bounded by `verify.auto_resume_max` (default 2, 0 disables; config-registry regenerated); attempts beyond the bound surface the existing failure with an attempts-count message (tested).\n- [x] Progress condition: a resumption dispatches only when the prior attempt strictly increased the cache-credited PASS count; unit tests cover (a) increasing count → resumes; (b) unchanged count → stops early with the failure surfaced, no further LLM run; (c) progress then stall → exactly one extra attempt.\n- [x] Resumption trail recorded per attempt (attempt number, cache-credited count, remaining count) and visible on the ticket or in the close output (tested).\n- [x] The loop sits at the shared gate seam: an MCP-or-library-path close exercises it in a test, not only the CLI path.\n- [x] Child idea ticket for frontier handoff created + linked discovered_from this ticket before this ticket closes.\n- [x] `make lint` / `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py","reason":"NEW: the bounded auto-resume loop wrapping llm.verify_completion (extracted helper at the shared close-gate seam)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"_completion_precheck seam: call the resume helper; FAIL message carries the attempts note"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"verify.auto_resume_max config key (default 2; 0 disables)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reason":"auto_resume_max coercer (int, minimum 0)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py","reason":"carry auto_resume_trail onto the durable COMPLETION_VERDICT record (PASS + FAIL branches)"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"document verify.auto_resume_max"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_close_autoresume_b5f8.py","reason":"RED-first tests: qualification reuse, bounds, progress rule, trail, shared-seam library path"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","66ac-42d2-c56f-4b1d"],["relates_to","b4be-0ed8-22cb-4b01"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f3e35448-6402-4c4e-aaad-39069fd5a751","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b5f8-d3f9-39d9-4195","ticket_type":"task","title":"Close gate auto-resumes verification on search exhaustion instead of failing to the operator","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2d710c81-3b40-4b45-b311-63735e9e1b33","516c181c-c7f5-4a2d-9e45-1f276cb3552e","20a9001b-7c29-4c12-9d71-7a0826c5ef54","19900069-eb67-4e6c-bafc-3c64c3a5727a","9cf082e7-0e52-49d7-b44c-77767634112f","3139268b-2a5d-4feb-860d-39ad74a69907","109acc53-6a97-4665-bb7f-69f8cfc8564d","6818d7f8-ea55-4ae6-9d50-b55c11f8fbbe","2ea41d74-ffb0-4a12-81e5-05d7609ec2df","161ce5b0-f924-45cd-baab-7326d5486e3e","5da9d3ee-e171-4ff6-bc9b-986aec6ac522","8de820db-83c9-4c31-89a7-090c5faf39b9","faebfe91-d5ad-4a3a-841a-cc32fba3f4a0","f3e35448-6402-4c4e-aaad-39069fd5a751","4c2b4444-d593-45d9-abff-74a9962b0c34"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786828303281158001,"uuid":"e9986809-d1db-412d-a307-aaf2b32c1de3"}